      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To file a roof insurance claim in Utah, call your insurance company's claims line or visit your Utah Insurance Department Home Claims Guide to report the damage and open a claim as soon as possible.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department Home Claims Guide",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "1. Get a Professional Inspection First"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Hire a reputable local roofer before calling your insurer."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ask for a detailed, photo-backed inspection report."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Confirm you have legitimate storm or hail damage worth filing against your deductible."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "2. Document the Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Take clear photos and videos of missing shingles, dented flashing, and granule loss in gutters."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Photograph interior leaks, wet insulation, or ceiling stains."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Write down the date, time, and type of storm (hail, heavy snow, or high wind)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "3. File the Claim"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Call your insurance carrier with your policy and claim details."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Write down your assigned claim number, filing deadlines, and the names of everyone you speak with."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Make temporary emergency repairs (like putting a tarp over a leak) to stop further damage, but save all receipts. Do not start permanent repairs yet."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "4. Meet the Adjuster"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Schedule a time for the insurance adjuster to inspect your roof."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ask your roofing contractor to attend this inspection so they can walk the roof with the adjuster and point out all damage ."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "5. Review the Payout and Complete Repairs"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Review the insurer's scope of work and estimate with your contractor to ensure nothing was missed."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Note that Utah policies often pay in stages\u2014an initial Actual Cash Value (ACV) check minus your deductible, followed by the remaining funds once the work is finished ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Choose any licensed Utah contractor you prefer to complete the work."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of storm caused the damage (hail, wind, heavy snow)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Do you know your deductible amount?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can share more details on what to expect during the adjuster meeting."
      },
